From: mediaforge
Subject: [PATCH] build: stop the install/uninstall hooks writing to OPENSSLDIR

LibreSSL's install-exec-hook installs cert.pem, openssl.cnf and x509v3.cnf
into $(DESTDIR)@OPENSSLDIR@ -- a path that ignores --prefix entirely. Its
uninstall-local counterpart removes the same three files from there.

mediaforge's default_install (lib/framework.sh:26; wired as the default
pkg_install at :69) runs a bare `make install`
with NO DESTDIR, so @OPENSSLDIR@ is used verbatim. That makes the hook actively
harmful the moment --openssldir points anywhere outside the build prefix.
Measured 2026-08-23 against LibreSSL 4.3.2, configured --with-openssldir=/etc/ssl:

    make            rc=0
    make install    rc=2
      install: cannot remove '/etc/ssl/cert.pem': Permission denied
      install: cannot remove '/etc/ssl/openssl.cnf': Permission denied
      install: cannot create regular file '/etc/ssl/x509v3.cnf': Permission denied

As an unprivileged user the recipe simply dies. Run as root it would instead
OVERWRITE the host's trust store and OpenSSL configuration, because upstream's
own no-overwrite guard does not work:

    for i in cert.pem openssl.cnf x509v3.cnf; do \
        if [ ! -f "$$OPENSSLDIR/$i" ]; then \

`$i` is a MAKE variable reference (single $), not the shell loop variable `$$i`,
and make expands it to the empty string. The guard therefore tests
`[ ! -f "$OPENSSLDIR/" ]` -- a directory, for which -f is always false -- so the
"already exists, install will not overwrite" branch is unreachable and every
run installs unconditionally. That is why the measured run above tried to
*remove* an existing /etc/ssl/cert.pem rather than skipping it. Reported
upstream; the typo is present in 4.3.2.

The same hazard does not reach the sibling mediaforge-meson port, because
meson's external_project always sets DESTDIR for the install step
(mesonbuild/scripts/externalproject.py:58), which redirects the hook into the
staging tree. mediaforge has no such redirection, so the lever available here is
to remove the hooks.

Nothing of value is lost: mediaforge does not want LibreSSL's bundled
configuration files installed by upstream's rules, and it places the CA bundle
itself in pkg_post_install so that the location is a decision the recipe makes
rather than a side effect of autotools' sysconfdir. `make uninstall` is never
invoked by mediaforge (uninstall is manifest-based, lib/install.sh), so
uninstall-local is unreachable in this build -- it is neutralised alongside
install-exec-hook because it is the same class of out-of-prefix write, not
because it currently fires.

TARGETS Makefile.in, NOT Makefile.am: the release tarball is an autotools *dist*
tarball shipping pre-generated Makefile.in, so patching the .am would be inert
without autoreconf.

--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -916,31 +916,10 @@
 install_sw: install
 
 install-exec-hook:
-	@if [ "@OPENSSLDIR@x" != "x" ]; then \
-		OPENSSLDIR="$(DESTDIR)@OPENSSLDIR@"; \
-	else \
-		OPENSSLDIR="$(DESTDIR)$(sysconfdir)/ssl"; \
-	fi; \
-	mkdir -p "$$OPENSSLDIR/certs"; \
-	for i in cert.pem openssl.cnf x509v3.cnf; do \
-		if [ ! -f "$$OPENSSLDIR/$i" ]; then \
-			$(INSTALL) -m 644 "$(srcdir)/$$i" "$$OPENSSLDIR/$$i"; \
-		else \
-			echo " $$OPENSSLDIR/$$i already exists, install will not overwrite"; \
-		fi \
-	done
+	@:
 
 uninstall-local:
-	@if [ "@OPENSSLDIR@x" != "x" ]; then \
-		OPENSSLDIR="$(DESTDIR)@OPENSSLDIR@"; \
-	else \
-		OPENSSLDIR="$(DESTDIR)$(sysconfdir)/ssl"; \
-	fi; \
-	for i in cert.pem openssl.cnf x509v3.cnf; do \
-		if cmp -s "$$OPENSSLDIR/$$i" "$(srcdir)/$$i"; then \
-			rm -f "$$OPENSSLDIR/$$i"; \
-		fi \
-	done
+	@:
 
 # Tell versions [3.59,3.63) of GNU make to not export all variables.
 # Otherwise a system limit (for SysV at least) may be exceeded.
